# Error And Logging Rules

Normalize failures and keep logs safe.

## Requirements
- Routes and services must throw typed or safe domain errors only.
- The global error middleware must map failures to the canonical problem-details response.
- Application logs must be structured and include request, tenant, facility, user, module, and action context when available.
- Secrets, access tokens, raw credentials, and PHI must be redacted.
- Audit logs must stay separate from application logs.
- Console noise and duplicate logging are defects.
